V1.1 RELEASE FEATURES
===========================================================================
- generalize Event to allow non-tracked characters to be event sources
    - happens when CC is used: the source is the target (or multiple targets, for AoE)
    - for AoE CCs: need to prevent adding tons of events for a single ability (one
      AoE cast = possibly many mobs fire UNIT_AURA->events)
- fold evidence tracking into Character

- fix the fiery brand 2-charge problem
    - requires a side effect-free inferAbility call to see if an update is
      plausibly an ability use (check things like button press, cooldown
      state, etc.) without clobbering `buff`'s state to allow inferAbility
      to run (i.e., startTime=now, certain=false).

- don't clear tracker data when party members join/leave/change positions
    - requires migrating current CD status tracking into Character and out of the
      icons that display the CDs. one reason this isn't trivial is polling: the icons
      register OnUpdate, so are constantly checking for changes, e.g., when a recharge
      completes

- UNIT_DIED handler. Seems the GUID is secret - probably fires for deaths
  of NPCs as well as players. PLAYER_DEAD also fires, has no payload. would
  be better than UNIT_DIED if that includes NPCs
    - combine with UNIT_FLAGS-based combatDrops

- Detect ability resets. E.g., detect when cold snap is used to reset ice cold/
  ice block.

- Minimap button
    - re-anchor frames to deal with sort changes
    - reset cooldown trackers

- Options
    - Font options for cooldown numbers
        - outlines, size, font
    - Support directional layouts other than horizontal+left of frame
    - Max history tray size
    - Show offensives on right
    - maybe add tooltips for confusing abilities like the DH apex talent
    - Options to augment the centerdefensivebuff icon:
        - Blizzard opts not to show buffs some would like to see. E.g.,
          bubble, evasion and meta.

- [PROBABLY LATER] Major debugging feature: export string with all trace data from e.g., a dungeon.
    - [In the short term, ignore everything below] Compressing data into a shareable string is great for
      debugging, but in the near term, an uncompressed record with an explorer will be very useful. The
      calculations below indicate that storing inference records without compression should be no problem.
    - Some ideas about compressing inference history into a shareable string
        - layout: one block per target guid, so every record in that block can be assumed to target
          the same guid without wasting storage space. when caster != target, encode guids
        - header: build guid encoding (e.g., slot indexes 1..5 in 3 bits).
        - inferAbility: make bit string of all logic layer and confidence network results
          for each inference call.
            - [maybe] record large data like timestamps only for failing logic elements or passing network elements
            - run length encoding for multiple inference calls made on the same data changes
                - how to deal with duration changing?
            - time stamp encoding? 4B=32b float probably. can an offset encoding help? if dungeon < 40m is the longest
              tracker, 40*60*1k is ~2.5M ms is the max offset, needs 22 bits. so 68% compression. maybe helpful.
        - game loop: store bit-compressed records of every aura with an interesting flag and a bit on
          whether they were correctly inferred. ~8 bits of flags, 3 bits for slot (5 man content). header flag can
          help 
        - quick and dirty calc: worst case is probably prot paladin with ~10 tracked cds, 1 CPM. so 30 min
          dungeon would be 300 inference requests. assume avg 3 inference attempts per success = 900 traced
          events. 10 bytes per inference (how realistic is that? one time stamp is 4B) = 9kB, so base 64 encoded
          would be a 12,000 character string. Not that bad.
    



